        "headline": "Correspondence per household: published values for FY2025 and how they moved.",
        "statements": [
          {
            "text": "In FY2025, Correspondence per household was 98.6 (pieces per household per year). That rose by 1.4 (1.4%) from the previous year, FY2024. That fell by 26.5 (21.2%) from five years earlier, FY2020.",
            "metric": "correspondence-per-household",
            "years": [
              2025,
              2024,
              2020
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "By income in FY2025, Correspondence per household (pieces per household per year) was highest for $150,000 and Over at 115.7 and lowest for Less than $50,000 at 90.8.",
            "metric": "correspondence-per-household",
            "years": [
              2025
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "By age in FY2025, Correspondence per household (pieces per household per year) was highest for 65 and Over at 130.4 and lowest for Under 45 at 71.5.",
            "metric": "correspondence-per-household",
            "years": [
              2025
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "By education in FY2025, Correspondence per household (pieces per household per year) was highest for Some college or technical school graduate at 102.7 and lowest for Less than high school at 83.9.",
            "metric": "correspondence-per-household",
            "years": [
              2025
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "By msa in FY2025, Correspondence per household (pieces per household per year) was highest for Non-MSA at 102.5 and lowest for Large MSA at 94.0.",
            "metric": "correspondence-per-household",
            "years": [
              2025
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "By tenure in FY2025, Correspondence per household (pieces per household per year) was highest for Own at 111.7 and lowest for Rent at 72.7.",
            "metric": "correspondence-per-household",
            "years": [
              2025
            ]
          }
        ],
        "caveats": [
          "Methodology change in FY2024: New contractor and per-household reporting. Comparisons across it should be cautious.",
          "Methodology change in FY2025: Household Mail Survey redesign. Comparisons across it should be cautious.",
          "Household-group bands (age, income, education) were redefined over time, so group comparisons across years should be read with the methodology notes."
